  "description": "TANLOM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C110 H96 N12 O16 S6 Tb4,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.592-3.867 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.13-111.60°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C117H100Tb4N15.50O16S6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
